From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jun Matsushita <jun@mercury.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:39:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] remote_execution: add the Build Event Service and Bazel
 BEP protocol crates

Three new crates hold the generated Rust for the protocols an OSS build event
service sink needs:

- bes_grpc_proto: google.devtools.build.v1, the Build Event Service.
- bazel_bep_proto: Bazel's build_event_stream and the messages it imports.
- google_grpc_proto: google.api, google.rpc, google.longrunning and
  google.bytestream, with the serde helpers for Any.

The Google protos move out of re_grpc_proto into google_grpc_proto, so the RE
and BES crates share one copy. re_grpc_proto re-exports `google`, so code
that names `re_grpc_proto::google::...` is unchanged.

Nothing uses the new crates yet.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
